# .TODO

This library originaly created in Debian 11 & 12.
Follow-up items deferred from the debug build fix on arch-based.

## shared library (libbehh.so) is disabled

Status: static-only build (BEHH_BUILD_SHARED=OFF in build-debug-full-linux.sh).

Why:
- the prebuilt /mnt/256a1/lib/libdrogon.a is non-PIC (built without -fPIC).
- it uses local-exec thread-local storage (relocation R_X86_64_TPOFF32).
- a non-PIC static archive with local-exec TLS cannot be linked into a shared
  object, so libbehh.so fails at link time.
- the static library, all tests, and tools build and link fine, they only ever
  use behh_static.

Next fix (to re-enable the shared library):
- rebuild drogon with position independent code, then install it:
    cd /mnt/256a1/repo/drogon
    cmake -B build -DCMAKE_POSITION_INDEPENDENT_CODE=ON <other flags>
    cmake --build build
    cmake --install build
- after a PIC libdrogon.a is in place, drop -DBEHH_BUILD_SHARED=false from
  build-debug-full-linux.sh (the option defaults ON).
- alternative: link drogon as a shared library instead of the static archive.

## notes for the contributor/maintainer

- the object core lib (add_library(behh OBJECT ...)) is what compiles the
  sources. dependency wiring done only on behh_static / behh_shared (the foreach
  loop) does NOT reach that compilation. anything that affects how the sources
  compile (include dirs, and PUBLIC compile definitions like
  ZXING_EXPERIMENTAL_API) must also be applied to the object lib, otherwise the
  headers and the linked library disagree on struct layout (ABI mismatch).
- test data files are resolved from BEHH_TESTS_DIR (absolute path injected by
  tests/CMakeLists.txt), so tests can run from any working directory.
